{
  "requirement": "The harness instructs the model to finish by calling\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission.mcp`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.submission` has one obligation. The harness must instruct the model to finish by calling `submit_result`. The tool's shape and schema belong to the cited `submission.mcp`, and acceptance belongs to `submission.acceptance`. Neither needs a test here.\n\n**Implementation.** The instruction comes from a single place: the prompt `format!` in `tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>]#2/fn[run_with_domain_tools]`. It says \"Finish by calling submit_result with {\"result\": ...}. Text alone is not a result.\" Every backend goes through it.\n\n**Tests.** Each of these asserts that the instruction actually reaches the model:\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` runs against a local transport. For all 4 captured OpenAI requests, it asserts that the serialized input contains \"Finish by calling submit_result\".\n- `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` does the same for both native Ollama chat requests. It asserts that the serialized messages contain the instruction.\n- `assistant_text_and_provider_failure_cannot_become_typed_results` asserts that the first request's chat history contains the instruction. It also checks that the reminder after a text-only reply says to invoke `submit_result` exactly once.\n\nThe two backend tests and the generic `ToolAgent` test together cover the instruction at the provider boundary. They would fail if the instruction were dropped or reworded.\n\nThe default-tool and typed-submission tests in `agent/tests.rs` also carry the `submission` marker. They check the `submit_result` tool and its schema, which is the `submission.mcp` side. They are not needed for the instruction itself.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The requirement states only one condition, so there are no distinct modes or boundary cases left untested.",
  "references": "6d3090f0bb60675c1ce9da3313f3f3f65297e0a05452744687240cd1bb853491",
